#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# normalized

#% text
# `normalized(v)` gives the vector `v` divided by its norm; `normalized(v, f)` gives `v/f(v)`. As an option of `histogram`, `normalized: true` scales the bars so that their total area is 1, a probability density.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The norm is `norm(v)`: the Euclidean length of a vector (with absolute values of complex entries), the 2-norm of a matrix, and `abs(z)` of a number `z`.

#% item
# A vector whose norm is 0 is returned as it is.

#% item
# With a function `f`, `v` may be any expression: a polynomial divided by an inner-product norm, say.

#% item
# The values of a `time_series` are normalized as one vector; the times stay.

#% item
# The option of `histogram` is `false` by default: the bar heights are the counts.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
normalized([1, 5, 1])
#% output
#= [(1/9)*3^(1/2), (5/9)*3^(1/2), (1/9)*3^(1/2)]

#% cell
normalized([x, y])
#% output
#= [x/(abs(x)^2 + abs(y)^2)^(1/2), y/(abs(x)^2 + abs(y)^2)^(1/2)]

#% cell
normalized(3 + 4*im)
#% output
#= 3/5 + 4*im/5

#% cell
seed(3); data = random_variate(normal_distribution(0, 1), 1000); histogram(data, normalized: true)
#% output
#= image("normalized.files/normalized-4.svgz")

#% cell
histogram(data, normalized: false)
#% output
#= image("normalized.files/normalized-5.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
normalized([[1, 2], [4, 5]], norm)
#% output
#= [[(23 + 2*130^(1/2))^(-1/2), 2/(23 + 2*130^(1/2))^(1/2)], [4/(23 + 2*130^(1/2))^(1/2), 5/(23 + 2*130^(1/2))^(1/2)]]

#% cell
normalized(1 + x + x^2, &(integrate(&1^2, [x, -1, 1])))
#% output
#= (5/22)*(1 + x + x^2)

#% cell
histogram(data, bins: [0.5], normalized: true)
#% output
#= image("normalized.files/normalized-8.svgz")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The density estimate beside the true density:

#% cell
show(histogram(data, normalized: true), plot(pdf(normal_distribution(0, 1), x), [x, -4, 4]))
#% output
#= image("normalized.files/normalized-9.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `norm`, `unit_vector`, `histogram`, `bins`, `pdf`
